3-13-23:
My servant CalebThe fulfillment of this promise appears in Joshua 14:6–15;
Judges 1:20.
Another spirit. That is, the influence of the Holy Spirit upon the personal spirit of
Caleb (see Judges 3:10; 6:34; Isa. 59:19; 61:1).
Followed me fully. This is repeated several times (see Joshua 14:8; Num. 32:11;
Deut. 1:36).

3-25-7:
The sonsPlural, even though there was but one son. It was the correct formula to
use even though it did not fit this precise instance (see also Gen. 46:23; 1 Chron. 1:41;
2:7; and Num. 26:36).

3-30-26:
Divide the preyThe entire camp had suffered at the hand of the Midianites;
therefore it was proper that the ones who had remained in camp should also receive a
share.

3-31-19:
Before the LordJehovah is looked upon as a God of battles, going before the
marching nation to confound their enemies (see Num. 21:14; Joshua 4:5, 11–13; 6:8, 9;
Judges 5:23).
